desc:MTT Loon
// Version: 0.30 - Loon (file and folder still named mtt_kellylochbaum_coupled). Asymmetric two-mass vocal folds (Ishizaka-Flanagan 1972; left/right
// asymmetry after Steinecke-Herzel 1995) coupled to a five-section Kelly-Lochbaum
// tract with an optional five-branch side-cavity junction, an optional second fold
// pair (voice 2, coupled to the first) and an air-sac supply drained by the glottal flow.
// No oscillator or wavetable makes the sound: pitch emerges from the folds and their
// interaction with the tract. Optional tremor and insert effects alter that motion
// and the radiated sound. Not an anatomical simulation.
// Inspiration: Jean-Edouard Miclot's (JED) Kyma creature voices and his patch
// "Kelly-Lochbaum Vocal Tract 7 junctions + 5 Radiis" (radiating side branches, L/R
// mixes with compression: the OUTPUT stage), and xoxos' Fauna (a five-segment KL tract
// coupled to a mass-spring glottis).
tags:instrument synthesis physical-modeling
in_pin:none
out_pin:Left
out_pin:Right
options:maxmem=8388608
import loon_fx.jsfx-inc
// Title icon, loaded from the effect's folder into image slot 0.
filename:0,loon.png
filename:1,loon_dark.png
filename:2,title.png
filename:3,title_dark.png
filename:4,wm.png
filename:5,wm_dark.png
